# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: setvar-validation-as-measured -- SETVAR range checks, ERRNO codes, return value and symbol names as AutoCAD / BricsCAD do
#+STATUS: DONE
#+PRIORITY: P2
#+TYPE: divergence
#+DEPENDS: windows-runner-sunset-probe-campaign
#+BRANCH: -
#+DATE: 2026-10-28

Measured by the sunset campaign's B4 probe (probe-setvar-edges.lsp,
2026-10-28: AutoCAD 2022 job 17540963671, BricsCAD V25 Windows 17540963675,
V26 macOS 17540963672); the table is in the spec's SETVAR "Tested
Behaviour". clautolisp:

1. checks no range: (setvar "CMDECHO" 2), (setvar "LUNITS" 7),
   (setvar "OSMODE" -1) are accepted, where both products refuse them
   (AutoCAD ERRNO 22, BricsCAD 0), leaving the variable unchanged; USERI1
   40000 is clamped to 32767 (AutoCAD refuses, BricsCAD wraps to -25536);
   OSMODE 70000 is kept (AutoCAD refuses, BricsCAD wraps to 4464). Needs the
   variables' ranges: in the sysvar catalogue, harvested where possible
   (sunset batch B5, the sysvar read-only and default sweep, is the place).
2. ERRNO: 1 for a read-only name (both: 20), 1 for an unknown one (both: 0),
   4 for a bad type (AutoCAD 87, BricsCAD 0).
3. returns the STORED value (CMDECHO 1.0 -> 1); both return the value GIVEN
   (1.0, and USERR1 2 -> 2).
4. refuses a symbol name: (setvar 'OSMODE 1) works on both.
5. CMDECHO 0.7: stored as 0 (BricsCAD's); AutoCAD refuses (ERRNO 87).
6. SNAPBASE '(1 2 3) on a 2D variable: stored 3D; AutoCAD refuses, BricsCAD
   keeps (1.0 2.0).
Product-specific points (2, 5, 6, the wrap) behind the dialect's product.

* B5 captured -- the ranges point 1 waited on (2026-11-16)

Sunset campaign B5 (probes/sources/probe-sysvar-flags.lsp, 546 cases),
captured 2026-11-16 by MR !548's probe:suite jobs: AutoCAD 2022 Windows (job
18078448045, probe-results/autocad/ms-windows/20261116T180525Z), BricsCAD
Windows (18078448049, .../bricscad/ms-windows/20261116T181223Z) and BricsCAD
macOS (18078448046, .../bricscad/macos/20261116T181026Z). Each range case is
(setvar NAME VALUE) just below, at and above a documented bound, restored
after; "ok" = stored as given, "stored N" = stored something else,
"refused ERRNO n" = an error.

Reading for point 1: for nearly every documented bound BOTH products refuse
the out-of-range value -- AutoCAD with ERRNO 22, BricsCAD with ERRNO 0 (the
same split as B4) -- so most rows below differ in the ERRNO only. Of
AutoCAD's 167 listed answers, 142 are refusals; the departures are the
"stored N" / "ok" rows, where a product coerces or accepts a value the
catalogue's :range excludes (e.g. DIMADEC -1 stored 2 on all three, BVMODE
-1 / 2 stored 1 on AutoCAD only): those variables need their measured range
in the catalogue. Rows where all three agree in full are not listed.
Point 1 can now be modelled: refuse outside the catalogue range with the
product's ERRNO, and the coercions above per product.

